---
import Base from "@/layouts/Base.astro";
import Icon from "@/components/Icon.astro";
import { site, about } from "@/data/site";
import { withBase } from "@/lib/url";
---

<Base
  title="About Me"
  description="Learn more about Mitchell Salzman, ECE student at the University of Minnesota, medical device builder, and founder of STRIVE Medical."
>
  <div class="about-page">
    <!-- Hero banner -->
    <section class="about-hero">
      <div class="about-hero-inner">
        <div class="about-hero-text">
          <p class="eyebrow mb-4">About Me</p>
          <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl">
            Hi, I'm Mitchell.
          </h1>
          <p class="mt-4 max-w-lg text-lg leading-relaxed text-body">
            I build things that are useful to people, mostly in medical devices
            and health tech, where the stakes are real and the person on the
            other end of the design matters.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="about-hero-image">
          <img
            src={withBase("/media/about/jml-0776.jpg")}
            alt="Mitchell Salzman in graduation regalia at the University of Minnesota"
            loading="eager"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Main flowing content -->
    <section class="about-body">
      <div class="about-flow">

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">My Story</h2>

        <!-- Awards + Hackathon float right -->
        <div class="float-right-pair">
          <div class="overlap-pair">
            <img
              src={withBase("/media/about/medtronic-hackathon.jpg")}
              alt="Mitchell's team at the Medtronic Hackathon presenting TAMORA"
              class="overlap-back"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <img
              src={withBase("/media/about/awards-ceremony.jpg")}
              alt="Mitchell presenting at an awards ceremony"
              class="overlap-front"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
          I study electrical and computer engineering at the University of
          Minnesota, on a combined bachelor's and master's track. That's the
          background, not really how I think about myself.
        </p>

        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
          What I care about most is building things that are useful to people.
          I like getting in early, when a problem is still messy, figuring out
          what's worth building, then helping make it real. That's the product
          side, and it's the part I love. Not just how something works, but why
          it exists, who it's for, and what makes them come back.
        </p>

        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
          The way I actually get there is systems thinking. I'm good at it,
          and I like it. Holding all the moving parts of a problem in view at
          once and seeing where they push and pull against each other. Project
          management is where that turns into something real for me, and I
          genuinely enjoy it: taking a messy pile of dependencies and shaping
          it into work a team can actually ship.
        </p>

        <div class="clear"></div>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Why Medical Devices</h3>

        <!-- Cleanroom pair float left -->
        <div class="float-left-pair">
          <div class="overlap-pair overlap-pair--flip">
            <img
              src={withBase("/media/about/cleanroom-wafer.jpg")}
              alt="Silicon wafer in the cleanroom"
              class="overlap-back"
              loading="lazy"
            />
            <img
              src={withBase("/media/about/cleanroom-suit.jpg")}
              alt="Mitchell in a cleanroom bunny suit"
              class="overlap-front"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Mostly I'm into medical devices and health tech. I like understanding
          how something is built, how it reaches the people who need it, and
          who it's really for, all at once, because in medical devices those
          three answers have to line up or the product never reaches anyone.
          Something technically impressive and clinically confused is still
          broken; it just takes longer for anyone to say so. What pulls me
          toward medical devices in particular is that the stakes are real.
          There's a person on the other end of the design, so the interesting
          question is rarely whether a thing <em>can</em> be done and almost
          always whether it <em>should</em> be, and for whom.
        </p>

        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Long term, I want to build products and eventually start my own
          company. Product management sits right where the technical, business,
          and people sides meet.
        </p>

        <div class="clear"></div>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">STRIVE Medical</h3>

        <!-- STRIVE photos float right as a 2x2 collage -->
        <div class="float-right-collage">
          <div class="strive-grid">
            <div class="strive-img strive-img--tall">
              <img
                src={withBase("/media/about/strive-presenting.jpg")}
                alt="Mitchell presenting STRIVE Medical project work"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
            <div class="strive-img">
              <img
                src={withBase("/media/about/strive-conversation.jpg")}
                alt="Mitchell chatting with STRIVE members at UMN"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
            <div class="strive-img">
              <img
                src={withBase("/media/about/strive-device.jpg")}
                alt="STRIVE members assembling a medical device at an event"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
            <div class="strive-img strive-img--tall">
              <img
                src={withBase("/media/about/strive-group.jpg")}
                alt="Full STRIVE Medical team group photo"
                loading="lazy"
              />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
          I started STRIVE Medical because I wanted to share the passion I have
          for the medical device industry, and because I wanted more people to
          feel confident in what they're actually capable of. At the end of the
          day, I want people to be able to walk into an interview and talk
          smart about the things they personally own and have contributed to,
          with the quiet confidence that only comes from having actually built
          the thing.
        </p>

        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
          What that looks like day to day is empowering my members: making them
          better public speakers, sharper researchers, prouder of what they
          build, and able to talk about it with real skill. When someone can
          speak with conviction about the thing they made, they stop feeling
          like they're along for the ride and start feeling like they're adding
          to what the whole group knows. A lot of it comes down to delegation,
          handing people real ownership and then pushing them a little further
          than they'd push themselves. But when you have people who actually
          care and want to get better, that push is usually all they need, and
          watching that development happen is the part I love most.
        </p>

        <div class="clear"></div>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Outside of Work</h3>

        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed mb-5">
          Weightlifting, motorcycling, snowmobiling and skiing, because a
          Minnesota winter may as well be good for something. Traveling around
          the world with my friends, trying to work on not overplanning. And
          camping, getting far enough out that the signal drops, and that's the
          point.
        </p>

        <!-- Personal photos row -->
        <div class="personal-grid">
          <div class="personal-img">
            <img
              src={withBase("/media/about/family-park.jpg")}
              alt="Mitchell with family in a park"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="personal-img">
            <img
              src={withBase("/media/about/friends-tapas.jpg")}
              alt="Mitchell with friends enjoying tapas abroad"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="personal-img">
            <img
              src={withBase("/media/about/hiking-trail.jpg")}
              alt="Hiking a trail with friends"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Quick facts -->
        <div class="facts-grid mt-10">
          <div class="fact-card">
            <span class="fact-label">Based in</span>
            <span class="fact-value">Minneapolis, MN</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fact-card">
            <span class="fact-label">Education</span>
            <span class="fact-value">BS + MS ECE, UMN</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fact-card">
            <span class="fact-label">Focus</span>
            <span class="fact-value">Medical devices & product</span>
          </div>
          <div class="fact-card">
            <span class="fact-label">Long term</span>
            <span class="fact-value">Build products, start a company</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Back link -->
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 pb-24 sm:px-12 md:px-24 text-center">
      <a
        href={withBase("/")}
        class="link text-sm inline-flex items-center gap-2"
      >
        <Icon name="arrow" size={14} class="rotate-180" /> back to portfolio
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-page {
    --about-max: 1120px;
  }

  .clear {
    clear: both;
  }

  /* ── Hero ── */
  .about-hero {
    padding: 9rem 1.5rem 4rem;
    background: var(--color-surface-alt, #f8fafc);
  }

  .about-hero-inner {
    max-width: var(--about-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 2.5rem;
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .about-hero-inner {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    }
  }

  .about-hero-image img {
    width: 240px;
    height: 320px;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: top;
    border-radius: 16px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    display: block;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 30px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .about-hero-image img {
      width: 280px;
      height: 380px;
    }
  }

  /* ── Main flowing body ── */
  .about-body {
    max-width: var(--about-max);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 4rem 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .about-body {
      padding: 4rem 3rem;
    }
  }

  .about-flow {
    max-width: 100%;
  }

  /* ── Float: right overlapping pair ── */
  .float-right-pair {
    float: right;
    width: 340px;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 1.5rem 2rem;
  }

  .float-left-pair {
    float: left;
    width: 320px;
    margin: 0.25rem 2rem 1.5rem 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .float-right-pair,
    .float-left-pair {
      float: none;
      width: 100%;
      margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
    }
  }

  /* ── Overlapping pair ── */
  .overlap-pair {
    position: relative;
    padding-bottom: 2.5rem;
    padding-right: 1.5rem;
  }

  .overlap-pair--flip {
    padding-right: 0;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .overlap-back {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 260px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  }

  .overlap-front {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    right: 0;
    width: 55%;
    height: 190px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border-radius: 10px;
    box-shadow: 0 6px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.18);
    border: 3px solid var(--color-surface, #fff);
  }

  .overlap-pair--flip .overlap-front {
    right: auto;
    left: 0;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .overlap-back {
      height: 300px;
    }
    .overlap-front {
      height: 220px;
    }
  }

  /* ── Float: right STRIVE collage ── */
  .float-right-collage {
    float: right;
    width: 440px;
    margin: 0.25rem 0 1.5rem 2rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .float-right-collage {
      float: none;
      width: 100%;
      margin: 0 0 1.5rem 0;
    }
  }

  .strive-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .strive-img {
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .strive-img img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 160px;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .strive-img--tall img {
    height: 200px;
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .strive-img img {
      height: 180px;
    }
    .strive-img--tall img {
      height: 230px;
    }
  }

  /* ── Personal photos row ── */
  .personal-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    clear: both;
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .personal-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
      grid-template-rows: 340px;
    }
  }

  .personal-img {
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line, #e2e8f0);
  }

  .personal-img img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 280px;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .personal-img img {
      height: 100%;
    }
  }

  /* ── Facts grid ── */
  .facts-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    clear: both;
  }

  .fact-card {
    padding: 1rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: var(--color-surface-alt, #f8fafc);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-line, #e2e8f0);
  }

  .fact-label {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--color-muted, #94a3b8);
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .fact-value {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-heading, #1e293b);
  }
</style>
